LAB 4 — Redline | CyberDefenders | Memory Forensics | Easy
Scenario
IDS alerted suspicious behavior on a workstation. Memory dump analyzed to trace malware actions and identify how attacker bypassed NIDS.
Malware Identified: oneetx.exe

Identified via windows.pslist — meaningless process name, ran multiple instances
PID 5896, PPID 8844 (parent already terminated — dropper cleaned itself up)
Wow64 = True — 32-bit process on 64-bit system, common malware technique
Spawned rundll32.exe as child process to execute malicious code

Memory Analysis

windows.malfind revealed PAGE_EXECUTE_READWRITE protection on oneetx.exe
MZ header found inside memory — confirmed process injection (fileless execution)
Hidden executable running inside oneetx.exe's memory space

VPN Bypass

Attacker installed Outline.exe — a legitimate VPN application
Outline.exe spawned tun2socks.exe to create network tunnel
This tunneled all traffic hiding it from NIDS detection
Attacker IP: 77.91.124.20

Tools Used: Volatility 3, windows.pslist, windows.netscan, windows.malfind
Concepts Learned: Process injection, MZ header detection, PAGE_EXECUTE_READWRITE, VPN bypass of NIDS, parent-child process relationships, Wow64

